Z||000011||FieroJoe||12-20-2001||02:21 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Rodney:<BR><B>I will soon be offering these same 304 stainless steel tips with 304 stainless steel exhaust pipes welded on for a direct replacement for GT style tips. List price looks to be about $75 each. I will also be using these for my new exhaust systems for the GT type rear bumpers. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I have never tried to put stock GT tips onto my Fiero, but what I want to know, is the pipe that connects the tip to the muffler different for the GT fascia, compared to my 87 coupe [Formula style] fascia?  I would like to have tips like those, especially if I can get it from Rodney with a stainless pipe welded right to it, so all I have to do is clamp it to my muffler.<P>Are they going to stick out too much because of that "intermediate" pipe's length?||||reg||1
